    "details": "OSS-Fuzz, Gary Gregory reports:\n\n> Uncontrolled Recursion vulnerability in Apache Commons Lang. This\n> issue affects Apache Commons Lang: Starting with\n> commons-lang:commons-lang 2.0 to 2.6, and, from\n> org.apache.commons:commons-lang3 3.0 before 3.18.0. The methods\n> ClassUtils.getClass(\\...) can throw StackOverflowError on very long\n> inputs. Because an Error is usually not handled by applications and\n> libraries, a StackOverflowError could cause an application to stop.\n> Users are recommended to upgrade to version 3.18.0, which fixes the\n> issue.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0488",
